---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { site } from '../data/site'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  updated="2 November 2026"
  description="How New Window Web Design collects, uses and protects personal information."
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {site.name} (“we”, “us”) handles personal information when you visit this website or contact
    us. We are an independent web design studio based in the United Kingdom, and we are the data controller for the
    information described here.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>When you send an enquiry through our contact form, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, business name and email address</li>
    <li>your existing website address, if you provide it</li>
    <li>the service you’re interested in and the details of your project</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When you use the website, our hosting provider processes technical information such as your IP address, browser type
    and the pages you request. We use this to deliver the website, keep it secure and prevent spam. To limit repeated
    form submissions, we store a one-way hash of your IP address for up to one hour; we do not store the address itself.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>to reply to your enquiry and discuss your project</li>
    <li>to prepare a quote and, if you go ahead, to deliver the work you’ve asked for</li>
    <li>to keep the website secure and protect our contact form from spam and abuse</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your information, and we do not use it for marketing unless you have asked us to.</p>

  <h2>Our lawful basis</h2>
  <p>
    We process enquiry information because it is necessary to take steps you have asked for before entering into a
    contract, and for our legitimate interests in responding to enquiries and running a secure website.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We use a small number of service providers who process information on our behalf:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website, protects it from abuse and provides the Turnstile spam check on our contact form.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers contact form enquiries to our email inbox.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these providers may process information outside the UK. Where they do, we rely on appropriate safeguards
    recognised under UK data protection law.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use advertising or analytics cookies. The Turnstile spam check on our contact form may process
    technical information about your browser and device so that it can tell people and automated bots apart; this is
    necessary to protect the form.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiries for as long as we need them to respond and, if you become a client, for as long as needed for our
    working relationship and to meet our legal and accounting obligations. We then delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under UK data protection law you can ask to access, correct or delete your personal information, ask us to restrict
    or stop using it, and ask for a copy in a portable format. To make a request, {
      site.email ? (
        <>
          email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          contact us through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>
        </>
      )
    }.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s
    Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when it was last changed.</p>
</LegalLayout>
